2026-10-23T21:33:25.7194424Z -- Provenance and the fail-closed Reconcile gate
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7201460Z   ok   a wave refuses to run without a committed roster
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7211181Z   ok   a roster that disagrees with origin stops the wave
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7211795Z   ok   a roster that is not the committed file stops the wave
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7212704Z   ok   a reconciler that returns nothing stops the wave
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7213026Z -- Resume stages
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7217680Z   ok   stage done reports merged and spends no agent
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7220014Z   ok   stage merge skips fixer AND reviewer
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7227512Z   ok   stage review skips the fixer only
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7231643Z   ok   a fixer that returns prose in `pr` is refused, after one retry
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7232131Z -- The stage vocabulary the rosters actually use
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7247993Z   scope  1 roster(s), 10 group(s), 2 distinct stage(s)
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7248717Z   ok   every resume.stage in every committed roster is one the wave script branches on
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7251248Z   ok   stage in-review is the review stage, and reads the roster's own open_pr key
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7252935Z   ok   stage pending starts a fixer, deliberately rather than by falling through
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7253708Z   ok   stage blocked spends no agent and is recorded for the orchestrator
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7257975Z   ok   an unrecognised stage refuses instead of starting a fresh fixer
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7258714Z -- The referent a keyed stage must carry, not only the stage word
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7262836Z   ok   every stage the wave script branches on has a decided referent, or a recorded exemption
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7269770Z   rule   review   derived head_sha + open_pr/pr        map head_sha + open_pr/pr   301 char(s) of branch source
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7270380Z   rule   merge    derived head_sha + pr                map head_sha + pr   197 char(s) of branch source
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7270775Z   rule   done     derived merge_sha + merged_pr        map merge_sha + merged_pr   313 char(s) of branch source
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7271159Z   rule   fix      derived pushed_sha                   map pushed_sha   404 char(s) of branch source
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7271502Z   rule   blocked  derived (exempt)                     map (exempt)   347 char(s) of branch source
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7272035Z   ok   every stage this map decides has a locatable branch in web-fix-wave.js
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7272662Z   ok   every key required here is one the branch that requires it actually reads
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7273109Z   ok   the map is exactly what the rule derives from the branch source
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7273448Z   ok   every bare resume key in a decided branch is classified by the rule
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7277531Z   scope  1 roster(s), 10 group(s), 9 in a stage that reads a key
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7277972Z   ok   every group in a stage the wave script reads a key for carries that key
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7278449Z   ok   the defect fires: `in-review` carrying only stage and note is refused
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7278833Z   ok   the repair passes: `in-review` carrying open_pr and head_sha is accepted (null control)
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7279156Z   ok   `done` discriminates in both directions on merged_pr / merge_sha
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7279505Z   ok   a stage the script reads no key for is not made to carry one (pending, blocked)
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7279952Z   ok   a null referent is a missing referent, not a present key
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7280509Z -- The verdict grammar, and the seats it dispatches
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7280731Z   ok   a well-formed merge verdict merges
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7281408Z   ok   a blocked verdict carries its class through to the result
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7281832Z   ok   a blocked verdict leaves a roster patch the orchestrator can apply
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7282212Z   ok   a blocked verdict is repaired once, then re-reviewed
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7283482Z   ok   a root-cause-unanswered verdict dispatches the root-cause seat, not another repair
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7284000Z   ok   the root-cause seat returns beside the fix, and the group stays unmerged
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7391648Z   ok   a root-cause-detectable verdict routes as itself, blocks, and dispatches the root-cause seat rather than a repair
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7400400Z   ok   the stats histogram keys root-cause-detectable as its own row, the same class the wave routes
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7403020Z   ok   a root-cause-unrecorded verdict routes as itself, blocks, and dispatches the root-cause seat rather than a repair
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7406806Z   ok   the stats histogram keys root-cause-unrecorded as its own row, the same class the wave routes
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7408432Z   ok   the reviewer prompt defines root-cause-detectable as a red a cheaper detector could have shown before the handoff
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7409047Z   ok   the reviewer prompt defines root-cause-unrecorded as a red whose cheapest detector is the check that went red
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7409826Z   ok   an unreadable verdict never merges, whatever the schema field says
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7410437Z   ok   an unreadable verdict is not retried as a repair request
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7411929Z   ok   a blocked verdict with an untaught class word parses and routes to other
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7412578Z   ok   and the untaught word survives in the why rather than vanishing into "unparseable"
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7413296Z   ok   an untaught class word is repaired once, exactly like a taught one -- the repair round is the proof the verdict ROUTED (unparseable verdicts skip it)
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7416362Z   ok   a bare blocked verdict (no class) parses and routes to other
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7416659Z   ok   a bare blocked verdict is repaired once, not discarded as unreadable
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7417530Z   ok   `blocked <sha>: <why>` parses with the reason kept as the why
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7418321Z   ok   a blocked verdict with a 39-hex SHA is still refused (#1106)
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7419602Z   ok   a `PASS — merge` line stays outside the grammar entirely
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7419954Z -- Regressions a review found, pinned so they cannot come back
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7420501Z   ok   a reviewer that returns nothing does not crash the group
2026-10-23T21:33:25.7420777Z   ok   ...and it is recorded as blocked, not as a thrown group
